Alexis <me@privacy.net> wrote:
>
> If the file format has not changed then there should be no real problem.  
> However, every time a new object / monster is added then bones files 
> would become incompatible since Hearse relies on the version stamp to 
> tell NH versions apart.  Could I suggest adding a few dozen dummy 
> objects and monsters to the next version?  This would allow you to make 
> such changes without any problems.

Dummy objects are no problem. There are already more objects that have
only description names than there are real objects.

But for monsters I'm not sure if this would be possible without
further code changes.

> Of course this would also require code to strip out any of these dummy 
> objects and monsters if loaded in a bones file.  I don't know if there 
> are any other problems that this might cause (e.g. in wandering monster 
> / random obj generation code).  Failing that, then all that's necessary 
> is to wait for major changes to settle down and then if there's demand 
> I'm happy to add support for UnNethack.

That's probably the best approach.

At the moment I couldn't guarantee that I can restrict myself in
regards of monsters and items and that dummy entries aren't
troublesome.

But I can guarantee that there won't be a release with an already
released version number that breaks save/bone-file compatibility. So
no 3.5.1.1 (if there will be one) that breaks 3.5.1 bones.

